 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Degenerate Tetrahedra:** If more than two cross-product tests return 1, the vertices are projected onto a line. These must be discarded to prevent artifacts [S1].
-*   **Sorting Accuracy:** Sorting by centroid is not 100% accurate. For perfect ordering, use Williams’ MVPO or k-buffer sorting [S1].
-*   **Perspective Distortion:** In perspective views, linear interpolation of extinction coefficient $\tau$ is an approximation because front and back faces have different perspective distortions. Hardware perspective-correct interpolation is insufficient for the average $\tau$ [S2, book].
-*   **Mach Bands:** Linear interpolation of integrated opacity $\alpha$ across the polygon is not mathematically equivalent to the exponential calculation, potentially causing Mach bands. Using a pre-computed texture for $e^{-\tau l}$ mitigates this [S2, book].
